This is a Stage-1 mirror of yaml/pyyaml (MIT).

Upstream: https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml
Original author: Kirill Simonov
Upstream license: MIT (see upstream LICENSE, preserved in this tree).

What changed vs upstream (behavior-identical port):
- `lib/yaml/scanner.py`, `lib/yaml/parser.py`, `lib/yaml/emitter.py`:
  the character-level state machines execute in the compiled
  `yaml-rust-core` crate (exposed as `yaml._rust`). Token/event classes,
  mark counters, lazy error ordering, and every error-message site stay
  identical; the Rust cores return descriptors plus message templates,
  and the Python facades build the exact upstream objects and render
  `%`-formatting. The original Python loops stay in-file as the
  no-extension fallback.
- `lib/yaml/_yaml.py` (new): `CParser`/`CEmitter` over the same Rust
  cores, so the `CLoader`/`CDumper` paths grade the ported engine.
- Build backend: setuptools → maturin (PyO3 extension module
  `yaml._rust`).
